WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.271 --> 00:00:22.616
Sage peeled a banana—her favorite after-practice snack—as she and her best friend, Lourdes, walked out of Park Gymnastics.

2
00:00:22.636 --> 00:00:30.100
"I can't believe the tryouts for Misty Blackwell's Gymnastics Camp are next Saturday," Sage said.

3
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.262
For three years in a row, she had tried out for the camp run by former Olympian Misty

4
00:00:36.322 --> 00:00:43.885
Blackwell. But Misty, a six-time gold medalist, only chose gymnasts with Olympic potential.

5
00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:49.067
Since Sage's last rejection, she had been preparing for this year's tryouts.

6
00:00:50.668 --> 00:00:55.670
Her parents thought she put too much pressure on herself, but going to the Olympics had been Sage's

7
00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:56.550
dream forever.

8
00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.412
"I'm so nervous about the tryouts," Lourdes said.

9
00:01:01.432 --> 00:01:05.794
"You're going to make it this year," Sage said firmly.

10
00:01:05.814 --> 00:01:08.755
"You're the best gymnast at Park.

11
00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:14.116
Besides, it's our last chance—we'll be too old next year.

12
00:01:14.136 --> 00:01:19.038
Plus, maybe the camp will help us catch up to Emi!"

13
00:01:20.238 --> 00:01:25.420
Emi Wilson was the top gymnast at Park's rival gym and had been to the camp three times

14
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:34.494
already. "There's a rumor that Emi's going to train overseas this summer, so she's not trying out," Lourdes

15
00:01:34.554 --> 00:01:37.897
said. Sage's face lit up.

16
00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:40.500
"Really?" She grinned.

17
00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:46.646
Emi's absence this year would definitely give Sage an advantage she had never had before.

18
00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:51.972
"I'll work extra hard this week to get one step closer to my dream!"

19
00:01:54.912 --> 00:01:59.855
When Sage and Lourdes arrived at the tryouts, the gym was packed with gymnasts and spectators.

20
00:02:01.416 --> 00:02:06.058
The girls joined the line at the registration table just as Misty Blackwell walked past.

21
00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:09.720
The famous gymnast stopped briefly to greet them.

22
00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:14.042
"I remember you two from last year—good luck with your tryouts."

23
00:02:15.783 --> 00:02:16.684
Sage froze.

24
00:02:16.704 --> 00:02:18.905
"Thank you, Ms.

25
00:02:18.945 --> 00:02:23.007
Blackwell!" "She remembered us!"

26
00:02:23.527 --> 00:02:24.148
Lourdes said.

27
00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.603
"I need to make sure that she remembers my performance too," Sage said.

28
00:02:31.864 --> 00:02:34.606
The girls took their seats and waited for the tryouts to start.

29
00:02:34.626 --> 00:02:40.169
"First up," the announcer called, "Emi Wilson."

30
00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:42.511
Lourdes gasped.

31
00:02:44.392 --> 00:02:45.693
"What's she doing here?"

32
00:02:45.713 --> 00:02:50.716
"I guess the rumors were wrong," Sage mumbled.

33
00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:59.284
As Sage watched Emi's performance, she could feel her anxiety mounting—Emi's technique was perfect.

34
00:03:00.745 --> 00:03:02.466
But Sage couldn't let it rattle her.

35
00:03:02.486 --> 00:03:08.770
"If Emi can give a perfect performance, so can you," she told herself sternly.

36
00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.393
"You've worked hard all week for this!"

37
00:03:13.654 --> 00:03:18.737
After Emi gave a final bow, the announcer called Sage to the floor.

38
00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:23.060
Lourdes flashed her a sympathetic look.

39
00:03:24.116 --> 00:03:26.497
"It stinks that you have to go right after Emi."

40
00:03:28.098 --> 00:03:29.519
Sage tried to brush it off.

41
00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:35.422
"I'm super prepared—Emi isn't the only one with Olympic potential."

42
00:03:35.442 --> 00:03:38.123
"That's the right attitude!"

43
00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:39.304
Lourdes grinned.

44
00:03:39.324 --> 00:03:41.065
"Good luck!"

45
00:03:43.887 --> 00:03:46.428
Sage walked onto the mat and breathed in deeply.

46
00:03:49.224 --> 00:03:54.486
As the music started, she raised her arms, striking a pose before tiptoeing backward to the edge of

47
00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:54.906
the mat.

48
00:03:56.386 --> 00:04:01.588
She was preparing for her first big move—a series of fast forward flips across the mat.

49
00:04:02.228 --> 00:04:07.009
But something instantly felt wrong Had her last step been too wide?

50
00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.950
Yes—and her heel had gone out of bounds!

51
00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:14.351
"Such a stupid mistake!"

52
00:04:14.692 --> 00:04:16.072
a voice in her head screamed.

53
00:04:18.808 --> 00:04:20.549
Quickly she tried to reassure herself.

54
00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:23.810
"You can make up for the error.

55
00:04:25.391 --> 00:04:27.852
Yesterday at practice your routine was perfect!"

56
00:04:29.572 --> 00:04:32.814
With that, Sage began her running start for the first flip.

57
00:04:34.114 --> 00:04:36.795
Suddenly everything seemed to move in slow motion.

58
00:04:37.836 --> 00:04:41.297
Her right foot wasn't in position her last step was awkward.

59
00:04:43.818 --> 00:04:45.379
She couldn't regain her balance.

60
00:04:46.979 --> 00:04:48.776
And then—bam!

61
00:04:48.796 --> 00:04:50.918
Sage flopped facedown onto the mat.

62
00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.663
Gasps rose from the crowd, and tears sprang to Sage's eyes.

63
00:04:58.044 --> 00:05:02.507
She wanted to get up and run away, but years of competing had taught her that quitting was

64
00:05:02.648 --> 00:05:03.448
not an option.

65
00:05:04.689 --> 00:05:06.931
As she picked herself up, the crowd applauded.

66
00:05:08.172 --> 00:05:11.815
She improvised a few poses, and then bravely continued her routine.

67
00:05:14.557 --> 00:05:19.613
After the tryouts Sage sat in a booth at Frosty Spoon, staring at Lourdes' certificate.

68
00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:27.116
Lourdes handed Sage a frozen yogurt, then discreetly slipped the certificate onto the seat, out of Sage's sight.

69
00:05:27.136 --> 00:05:31.077
"Even the best gymnasts fall," Lourdes said.

70
00:05:33.698 --> 00:05:34.399
Sage sighed.

71
00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:35.919
"I know.

72
00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:41.161
But even if I hadn't fallen, I wouldn't have gotten into Misty's camp."

73
00:05:41.181 --> 00:05:44.143
"What?" Lourdes said.

74
00:05:44.163 --> 00:05:50.086
"But you were so prepared, and you've done so well in competitions this year."

75
00:05:50.107 --> 00:06:00.395
"True," Sage agreed, "but there were lots of amazing gymnasts today—including you—all more talented than I am.

76
00:06:02.077 --> 00:06:05.320
My dream probably wasn't very realistic after all."

77
00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.443
"But it's good to dream big!"

78
00:06:09.864 --> 00:06:10.905
Lourdes protested.

79
00:06:10.925 --> 00:06:18.097
"Dreams are great," Sage said, "but not all dreams can come true."

80
00:06:18.117 --> 00:06:21.880
"Does this mean you're going to quit gymnastics?"

81
00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:29.004
"I'm not sure what it means yet," Sage said, "but I won't quit."

82
00:06:30.485 --> 00:06:32.446
Lourdes looked sad and uncomfortable.

83
00:06:35.348 --> 00:06:42.432
"I'm disappointed about my poor tryout," Sage added quickly, "but you know what—I'm going to be fine.

84
00:06:43.916 --> 00:06:47.981
Gymnastics might even be more fun without all the pressure I've been putting on myself."

85
00:06:48.001 --> 00:06:51.364
"Good point," Lourdes said.

86
00:06:52.986 --> 00:06:55.829
Sage dipped her spoon into the bowl of frozen yogurt.

87
00:06:55.849 --> 00:07:02.156
"Mmm," she said, smiling, "it's my favorite
